<section class="workbench" id="sound-analyzer" aria-label="Sound analyzer controls">
  <noscript><p class="notice">Enable JavaScript to analyze audio in your browser.</p></noscript>
  <div class="input-panel">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Choose your sound</span><h2>Listen closer.</h2><p>Your microphone or an audio file. Everything is processed here, in your browser.</p></div>
    <div class="controls">
      <button id="start-mic" type="button" class="primary">Analyze live sound</button>
      <label class="file-button" for="audio-file">Open audio file<input id="audio-file" type="file" accept="audio/*,.wav,.mp3,.m4a,.ogg,.webm,.flac" /></label>
      <button id="stop-analysis" type="button" disabled>Stop</button>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Files: up to 60 seconds / 20 MB. Stereo files: channel 1 is analyzed; playback retains both channels.</p>
    <p id="analyzer-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready. Your microphone is off.</p>
    <p id="analyzer-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
    <div class="record-controls"><button id="record-audio" type="button" disabled>Record clip</button><span id="recording-status" class="small">Optional recording · up to 55 seconds</span></div>
    <div id="playback-panel" hidden><label for="audio-playback">Clip playback</label><audio id="audio-playback" controls preload="metadata"></audio><div class="controls"><a id="download-audio" class="text-link" download="workshopgirl-recording.webm">Download clip</a><button id="clear-audio" type="button">Clear clip</button></div><p class="small">Playback does not move the charts: imported and recorded clips show a whole-clip analysis.</p></div>
    <details><summary>Measurement settings</summary><label for="fft-size">FFT size</label><select id="fft-size"><option value="2048">2048 · faster response</option><option value="4096" selected>4096 · balanced</option><option value="8192">8192 · finer frequency bins</option></select><p class="small">Hann window · no spectral smoothing · DC removed. Larger windows separate nearby tones better but cover more time. Change settings before starting a new measurement.</p></details>
  </div>
  <div class="measurement-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / Measure &amp; understand</span><h2>The sound, made visible.</h2></div><span id="source-label" class="source-tag">No source</span></div>
  <div class="metrics" aria-label="Current measurements">
    <div><span>Strongest spectral peak</span><strong id="dominant-frequency">—</strong><small>Not necessarily the fundamental</small></div>
    <div><span>Digital RMS level</span><strong id="rms-level">—</strong><small>dBFS · not acoustic dB SPL</small></div>
    <div><span>Frequency bin spacing</span><strong id="frequency-resolution">—</strong><small id="sample-details">Actual decoded / device sample rate</small></div>
  </div>
  <p id="measurement-note" class="small">Start a measurement to see numerical results.</p>
  <div class="chart-grid">
    <figure class="chart"><figcaption><h3>Waveform</h3><span id="waveform-caption">Digital amplitude / time</span></figcaption><canvas id="waveform-chart" role="img" aria-label="Waveform: digital amplitude versus time. Numerical RMS level is provided above."></canvas></figure>
    <figure class="chart"><figcaption><h3>Frequency spectrum</h3><span>Tonal dBFS / frequency (Hz, log scale)</span></figcaption><canvas id="spectrum-chart" role="img" aria-label="Frequency spectrum. Significant peaks and band energy are listed below."></canvas></figure>
    <figure class="chart wide"><figcaption><h3>Spectrogram</h3><span>Frequency (Hz, log scale) / elapsed time</span></figcaption><canvas id="spectrogram-chart" role="img" aria-label="Spectrogram showing how frequency content changes over time; brightness represents tonal level."></canvas><div class="legend"><span>Quiet −100 dBFS</span><span class="color-scale" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>0 dBFS</span></div><p class="small">Live view uses sampled frames, not continuous recording. File view includes every analysis frame. Dark areas are quieter; bright bands show stronger frequencies.</p></figure>
  </div>
  <div class="readouts"><section><h3>Significant peaks</h3><p class="small">Up to six separated peaks above a conservative relative threshold. These are spectral features, not a diagnosis.</p><ol id="peak-list"><li>No measurement yet.</li></ol></section><section><h3>Frequency-band energy</h3><p class="small">Share of total AC spectral power. Bands below 20 Hz or above 20 kHz are excluded, so values may total less than 100%.</p><ul id="band-list"><li>No measurement yet.</li></ul></section></div>
  <section class="comparison"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Compare</span><h2>Before. After. Side by side.</h2><p>Capture a stopped live frame or a whole-file average into A and B. Use the same microphone, position, gain, FFT settings and operating conditions.</p><div class="controls"><button id="save-a" type="button" disabled>Save result as A</button><button id="save-b" type="button" disabled>Save result as B</button><button id="clear-comparison" type="button" disabled>Clear A/B</button></div><p id="comparison-summary" role="status">No snapshots saved. Snapshots stay in this tab and are lost on reload.</p><div id="comparison-results" hidden><p class="small"><span class="key-a">Pink: A</span> · <span class="key-b">Blue: B</span> · tonal dBFS / Hz (log scale)</p><canvas id="comparison-chart" role="img" aria-label="Overlaid spectra of snapshots A and B. Differences are also listed in the comparison table."></canvas><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>A/B measurement comparison</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Measurement</th><th scope="col">A</th><th scope="col">B</th></tr></thead><tbody id="comparison-table"></tbody></table></div></div></section>
</section>
<script>
  import { mountAnalyzer } from './controller';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#sound-analyzer');
  if (root) mountAnalyzer(root);
</script>
